WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.370
At the health check, sixty of us

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.250
had our heights measured.

3
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.350
Sixty numbers in a long list.

4
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.990
Nobody could see anything in them.

5
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.920
So we drew their shape.

6
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.480
Today: how a histogram shows

7
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.780
the shape of your data.

8
00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.910
A distribution tells you how

9
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.710
often each value happens.

10
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.640
Are most pupils near the middle height?

11
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.530
Are there many very tall or

12
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.670
very short pupils?

13
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.480
That is the shape of the data.

14
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.220
A histogram groups the

15
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.740
values into equal bins.

16
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.500
Here each bin is five centimetres wide:

17
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.120
one forty to one forty five, one forty

18
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.340
five to one fifty, and so on.

19
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.390
Then we count how many

20
00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.990
pupils fall in each bin.

21
00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.730
Each bar is one bin, and its

22
00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:52.830
height is the count.

23
00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:56.550
Our bars rise to a peak in the middle and

24
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.030
fall away on both sides, like a hill.

25
00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.430
A shape like this is called symmetric.

26
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.240
The two sides look alike, so the mean

27
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.060
and the median are almost the same.

28
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.900
Heights, shoe sizes and many

29
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.580
test marks look like this.

30
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.490
Journey times look different.

31
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.310
Most pupils live close, but a

32
00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.750
few travel for an hour.

33
00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.850
The bars bunch on the left with

34
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.310
a long tail to the right.

35
00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:30.020
This is skewed right, and the tail

36
00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.360
pulls the mean above the median.

37
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.080
Quick check!

38
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.760
The journey times are skewed right.

39
00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.070
Which middle describes a

40
00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.150
typical pupil better?

41
00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:41.880
The median.

42
00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.440
The few long journeys pull the

43
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.660
mean up, so the mean is longer

44
00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.220
than most pupils' journeys.

45
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.800
The median stays with the typical pupil.

46
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.510
In the app, open Build a histogram.

47
00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.160
Change the bin width from one to twenty.

48
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.190
Too few bins hide the hill, and

49
00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.210
too many make a jagged comb.

50
00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.030
Your turn.

51
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.320
In a histogram of test marks, what

52
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.860
does the height of each bar show?

53
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.580
How many pupils got marks in that bin.

54
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:19.360
Remember: equal bins, bars that count, and

55
00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.020
a shape that is symmetric or skewed.

56
00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.210
The shape tells you which middle to trust.

57
00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.610
Try it yourself: measure the hand

58
00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.470
spans of your family or friends,

59
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.370
and put them in equal bins.

60
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.530
Draw the histogram and ask: is it a

61
00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:37.470
hill, or does it have a tail?
